{
  "_comment": "Canonical SysML node-type palette — the SINGLE source of truth for the diagram's colour-by-type mode, shared by the Rust side (smlml_view::palette) and the web/VS Code diagram (imported directly into palette.ts). Do not fork these values into CSS or TS literals. Family hues are mixed against the editor background at render time (≈20% fill / 65% border) so the same hue reads on light and dark themes; the values here are the pure family hues. NOTE: edge kinds are intentionally NOT encoded here — both renderers follow the OMG pilot SysML2PlantUMLStyle for edges (solid generalization family carrying an arrowhead glyph, dotted dependency/annotation, thick connection/binding), which is glyph/weight-based, not colour/dash-based.",
